  "body": "## Problem\n\nThe heavy test `the_users_bore_roughs_adaptive_level_by_level_and_verifies_clean` in `crates/app/tests/pocket3d_hsm.rs` pins an exact (moves, planar feeds, arcs) triple for each measured platform.\n\nPR #2013 (issue #2004) removed the depth level at Top Z (Z 20). This level cut only air on the stock face. The triples of Windows and Linux are measured again:\n\n- Windows x86_64, release: `(4716, 4688, 549)`.\n- Linux x86_64, release (cut runner, run 44127297984): `(4726, 4698, 549)`.\n\nNobody can measure macOS aarch64 now. The old macOS triple `(16026, 15382, 1413)` is stale. macOS now uses the \"not measured\" band arm of `bore_path_matches`.\n\n## Work\n\n1. On Apple silicon, run in release, two times:\n   `cargo test --release -j 6 -p camcraft-app --test pocket3d_hsm -- --ignored --exact the_users_bore_roughs_adaptive_level_by_level_and_verifies_clean --nocapture`\n2. Make sure that the two triples are the same.\n3. Add an exact `macos` / `aarch64` arm to `bore_path_matches` with the triple. Give the commit and the date in its comment.\n",
